Dockerfile
.dockerignore
node_modules
**/node_modules
npm-debug.log
README.md
# TypeScript's incremental state from a local `tsc` (tsconfig has
# `incremental`): the builder type-checks from scratch.
*.tsbuildinfo
# All of it: the builder compiles its own. Re-including a local
# .next/static and .next/standalone only shipped ~42 MB of a laptop's last
# build into every local build context.
.next
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Environment files - NEVER ship secrets in the image
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# IDE / editor
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo

# Documentation: nothing the build reads. Patterns are anchored at the
# context root, so `docs/` is the repository's docs/, NOT src/content/docs
# (the MDX of the /docs pages, which the build prerenders). The site's
# content is .mdx (next.config.mjs traces src/content/**/*.mdx), which
# `*.md` does not match; a .md the build ever reads needs a `!` line here.
docs/
**/*.md

# Tests and their tooling: nothing the build imports (tsconfig's **/*.ts
# would only type-check them for nothing).
tests
playwright-report
test-results
playwright.config.*
playwright.*.config.*
vitest.config.*
vitest.*.config.*
stryker.config.*
reports
.stryker-tmp

# Dev scripts
scripts/optimize-images.js

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Configuration of CI and editor tools that `next build` never reads (it
# reads package.json, next/tsconfig/tailwind/postcss configs and
# .eslintrc.json). Out of the context, an edit to them no longer changes
# `COPY . .` and rebuilds the whole app for identical output.
.trivyignore
.gitleaks.toml
audit-ci.jsonc
.releaserc
.prettierrc
.prettierignore
.editorconfig
.gitattributes

# Misc
coverage
**/*.log
